  "date": "2021-04",
  "title": "Informationen Zu Oeffnungszeiten Und Angeboten Der Eth Bibliothek Ab Dem 26 April 2021",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "Locations and opening hours",
      "text": "- InfoCenter and Circulation Desk in the ETH main building:\n\n- Architecture and Civil Engineering Library (Hönggerberg):\n\n- From Monday, 17 May 2021, all other library locations will also reopen Mon–Fri 09.00–18.00 and the Hönggerberg Depot Library Mon–Fri 09.00–17.00.\n\n- Loans and returns are possible again at all locations. Short searches and consultations can also take place in compliance with distance and hygiene regulations.\n\n- We offer a free postal service for ETH staff.\n\n- Reading lounges with national and international (specialist) journals and daily newspapers are available.\n\n- Photocopiers and scanners can be used in compliance with the distancing rules.\n\nFrom Monday, 26 April 2021, the following opening hours apply:"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Collections, archives and exhibitions",
      "text": "The Reading Room Collections and Archives and the exhibition of the Max Frisch Archive are regularly open Mon–Fri from 10.00–17.00. For the Reading Room pre-registration is kindly requested. The Thomas Mann Archives are accessible by appointment. The exhibition of the Graphische Sammlung can be visited during regular opening hours Mon-Sun from 10.00–16.45."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Events",
      "text": "Events are partly taking place on location again. Please read the notes and details about upcoming events in the events calendar."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Face masks mandatory",
      "text": "Face masks must be worn in all ETH buildings. The social distancing and hygiene measures of the Federal Office of Public Health (FOPH) remain in place. Please bear this in mind when visiting the ETH Library.\n\nYou can also continue to make use of our digital resources and contact options . Please do not visit the library if you belong to an at-risk group or are feeling unwell."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Subscribe to Newsletter",
      "text": "Any questions? The ETH Library will be happy to help.\n\nE-mail: You can also get in touch with us via WhatsApp or our chat function."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Staffnet",
      "text": "#ETHLibraryDigital – The ETH Library is there for you digitally with various resources and services , not only during the COVID-19 protective measures.\n\n#KnowMore – The prepared content issued by the ETH Library is at your free disposal and gives you a head start."
    }
  ],
